linux-firewall-kmod (2.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 2.2.0 (tag v2.2.0)
  * Kernel-space IP banning via netfilter hooks; decisions stay in user space
  * Jail system for multi-service isolation
  * Go regexp (RE2) log parsing in the daemon, no PCRE2, no JIT
  * Up to 10 regex patterns per jail (config.MaxRegexPatterns)
  * Ban table capacities are module parameters (fw_max_ban_entries and friends)
  * Permanent bans live in the kernel ban table and come back from the module
    state snapshot (state_file); SQLite holds ban history only
    (defaults.history_db_path, empty means the history DB is off)
  * Prometheus metrics export

